-- title:
--   Mod-3 weight window: weight at most four up to twist
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$ whose mod-$3$ representation is irreducible in the sense of `ModRepIsIrreducible`, i.e. the $3$-torsion subgroup of the points of $W$ over an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ is nontrivial and its only Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/3$-submodules are $0$ and the whole module. Let $N'$ be a nonzero natural number with $3 \nmid N'$ admitting a prime divisor $q$ with $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$, let $S_0$ be a finite set of natural numbers with $3 \in S_0$, let $k \geq 2$ be an integer and $i$ a natural number. Write $\mathbb{T}(N',k,S_0)$ for `heckeAlgebra N' k S₀`, the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_k(\Gamma_0(N'))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N'$ with $\ell \notin S_0$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N'$ with $q \notin S_0$. Assume $\mathfrak{m}_k \subseteq \mathbb{T}(N',k,S_0)$ is a maximal ideal containing $3$ and containing $T_\ell - \ell^{i} a_\ell(W)$ for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$, where $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#(W \bmod \ell)$. Then there are an integer $k'$ with $2 \leq k' \leq 4$, a natural number $j$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}'$ of $\mathbb{T}(N',k',S_0)$ containing $3$ and containing $T_\ell - \ell^{j} a_\ell(W)$ for all those same primes $\ell$.
--
--   This is the $p = 3$ case of the weight bound for mod-$p$ eigensystems à la Edixhoven and Ash–Stevens: after a cyclotomic twist the occurring weight may be taken in the window $2 \leq k' \leq 4$, the hypothesis that $N'$ has a prime factor $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$ substituting for the Hasse invariant at level $N'$. It feeds the subsequent normalisation of the weight and exponent in [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_weight_le_succ_pow_mul_of_pow_mul_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_weight_le_succ_pow_mul_of_pow_mul_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_three_weight_le_four_pow_mul_apOfModel_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two.lean

